      "start": 7,
      "end": 7,
      "disposition": "implemented",
      "interpretation": "Qualifying ratifications alone are candidates for automatic approval. The tenant-scoped maximum of two and boundary-wide maximum of six use inclusive 86,400-second windows and select approved automatic ratification history. The tenant is the reviewed league value shared across its referees. Championship requests and qualifying requests over either limit use one league-supervisor approval.",
      "draft_paths": [
        "/actions/0/approval",
        "/runner_evidence/actions/league.result_ratification/automatic_limits",
        "/runner_evidence/actions/league.result_ratification/automatic_limits/0/history_selector/capability",
        "/runner_evidence/actions/league.result_ratification/automatic_limits/1/history_selector/capability",
        "/runner_evidence/runtime_contract/approval",
        "/runner_evidence/runtime_contract/approval_counter_selection"
      ],
      "operator_clarification": "For this new two-behavior revision, apply the automatic limits only to ratifications: two per league and six overall in the rolling 24 hours, retaining the existing ratification approval history. Withdrawals always require supervisor review and do not consume or expand those automatic ratification allowances. Keep every other ratification, withdrawal and Read requirement unchanged.",
